ial later plays\n   - Gives my teammate a chance to respond with their remaining cards\n\nReason:\nI should play ♦10 to beat the landlord\'s ♦9. This accomplishes several goals: it prevents the landlord from gaining control, it breaks up my pair of 10s (which is harder to play as a pair anyway), and it keeps my higher Jacks paired for potential strategic use. With my teammate holding only 3 cards, we need to maintain pressure on the landlord and give my teammate opportunities to play. Playing ♦10 is a balanced move that doesn\'t waste my highest cards while still competing effectively.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦10"]}'}
